  <img decoding="async" width="768" height="432" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/fears-768x432-1.jpg" class="attachment-medium_large size-medium_large wp-post-image" alt="Crypto Fear and Greed Index Taps Low at 'Extreme Fear,' BTC Technicals Point to Uncertainty" loading="lazy" style="float:left; margin:0 15px 15px 0;" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/fears-768x432-1.jpg 768w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/fears-300x169.jpg 300w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/fears-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/fears-696x385.jpg 696w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/fears-1068x601.jpg 1068w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/fears-747x420.jpg 747w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/fears-190x107.jpg 190w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/fears-380x214.jpg 380w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/fears-760x428.jpg 760w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/fears.jpg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px" /></p> 
  
  <p>
    <strong>On Wednesday, following the drop below the $30,000 region, bitcoin’s price has rebounded more than 8% since Tuesday’s low. Meanwhile, the sentiment metric recorded by the Crypto Fear and Greed Index (CFGI) is extremely low, pointing to “extreme fear” in the market. Despite being a scary term, the time is usually the best time to obtain assets for a lower price. However, data from Tradingview’s technicals show bitcoin is still in the “sell” range, while bitcoin market oscillators are more “neutral.”</strong>
  </p>
  
  <h2>
    CFGI Sentiment Metric Reaches ‘Extreme Fear’
  </h2>
  
  <p>
    The price of bitcoin (BTC) tapped a low of $29,300 on July 20, 2021, and since then the price has managed to jump back above the $32,000 handle. Despite the rebound, there’s a lot of uncertainty within the crypto space as far as short-term bitcoin price predictions are concerned.
  </p><figure id="attachment_476268" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-476268" style="width: 2880px" class="wp-caption aligncenter">
  
  <img decoding="async" srcset="https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/screen-shot-2021-07-21-at-12-21-18-pm-300x188.png 300w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/screen-shot-2021-07-21-at-12-21-18-pm-768x480.png 768w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/screen-shot-2021-07-21-at-12-21-18-pm-1024x640.png 1024w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/screen-shot-2021-07-21-at-12-21-18-pm-1536x960.png 1536w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/screen-shot-2021-07-21-at-12-21-18-pm-2048x1280.png 2048w, https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/screen-shot-2021-07-21-at-12-21-18-pm.png 2880w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 2880px) 100vw, 2880px" loading="lazy" class="wp-image-476268 size-full" title="Crypto Fear and Greed Index Taps Low at 'Extreme Fear,' BTC Technicals Point to Uncertainty" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/screen-shot-2021-07-21-at-12-21-18-pm.png" alt="Crypto Fear and Greed Index Taps Low at 'Extreme Fear,' BTC Technicals Point to Uncertainty" width="2880" height="1800" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-476268" class="wp-caption-text">BTC/USD chart shows bitcoin managed to climb back above the $32K zone on Wednesday.</figcaption></figure> 
  
  <p>
    Some believe the price may plunge to the $20,000 zone again and others believe a rebound is in the cards and the next trajectory will be well above the $64K all-time high. Most traders who believe this rebound could happen, think that today’s bitcoin price movements are eerily similar to the prices BTC saw in 2013. At that time, BTC plunged to $50 per coin after skyrocketing well above the $200 handle in mid-May 2013.
  </p>
  
  <p>
     
  </p><figure id="attachment_476271" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-476271" style="width: 1280px" class="wp-caption aligncenter">
  
  <img decoding="async" srcset="https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/fersd-300x169.jpg 300w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/fersd-768x432.jpg 768w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/fersd-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/fersd.jpg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px" loading="lazy" class="wp-image-476271 size-full" title="Crypto Fear and Greed Index Taps Low at 'Extreme Fear,' BTC Technicals Point to Uncertainty" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/fersd.jpg" alt="Crypto Fear and Greed Index Taps Low at 'Extreme Fear,' BTC Technicals Point to Uncertainty" width="1280" height="720" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-476271" class="wp-caption-text">Crypto Fear and Greed Index (CFGI) hosted on the website alternative.me on July 21, 2021.</figcaption></figure> 
  
  <p>
    Bitcoin’s price then jumped close to 2,400% after the summer 2013 low, and surged to the crypto asset’s first four-digit USD all-time high. After BTC dropped to $29,300 on Tuesday, the Crypto Fear and Greed Index (CFGI) tapped a low of ten on the charts. The score of ten is not the lowest point the CFGI metric has recorded but it is very low in comparison to most days. The last time the CFGI metric recorded a ten was in mid-June and at the end of May as well. Since the end of May, the CFGI metric hasn’t been this low in over a year as the last time the CFGI hit a ten or lower was during the March 12, 2020 market rout, otherwise known as ‘Black Thursday.’
  </p>
  
  <p>
    While the extreme fear sentiment may seem dismal, traders believe it is one of the best entry points to get into any market. A market filled with panic sellers and “extreme fear” is sure to see cheaper assets than one filled with “extreme greed,” which is the highest end of the CFGI spectrum. Essentially the CFGI analyzes “emotions and sentiments from different sources and crunches them into one simple number,” the website details.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <!-- growjs zone placement 31 -->
    
    <ins> <ins class="growjs-placement"></ins> </ins> <!-- end of growjs zone placement -->
  </p>
  
  <h2>
    Oscillators and Moving Averages Tell a Similar Story
  </h2>
  
  <p>
    In contrast to the CFGI, Tradingview’s BTC/USD technicals show a similar story but some of the indicators can be perceived as a different outlook. A single-day summary of Tradingview’s BTC/USD technicals shows a scale toward the “sell” range.
  </p><figure id="attachment_476275" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-476275" style="width: 1280px" class="wp-caption aligncenter">
  
  <img decoding="async" srcset="https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/technicals-300x169.jpg 300w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/technicals-768x432.jpg 768w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/technicals-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/technicals.jpg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px" loading="lazy" class="wp-image-476275 size-full" title="Crypto Fear and Greed Index Taps Low at 'Extreme Fear,' BTC Technicals Point to Uncertainty" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/technicals.jpg" alt="Crypto Fear and Greed Index Taps Low at 'Extreme Fear,' BTC Technicals Point to Uncertainty" width="1280" height="720" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-476275" class="wp-caption-text">Tradingview’s BTC/USD technicals on July 21, 2021, at 12:00 p.m. (EDT).</figcaption></figure> 
  
  <p>
    Moving averages (MA) are different and Tradingview’s MA technicals point to the “strong sell” range. Alongside this, BTC/USD oscillators are a bit warmer and are indicating a “neutral” range. For instance, the relative strength index (RSI 14) shows “neutral” and stochastic (14, 3, 3) also indicates things are “neutral.”
  </p><figure id="attachment_476273" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-476273" style="width: 1280px" class="wp-caption aligncenter">
  
  <img decoding="async" srcset="https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/btcssdd-300x94.jpg 300w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/btcssdd-768x240.jpg 768w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/btcssdd-1024x320.jpg 1024w, https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/btcssdd.jpg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px" loading="lazy" class="wp-image-476273 size-full" title="Crypto Fear and Greed Index Taps Low at 'Extreme Fear,' BTC Technicals Point to Uncertainty" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/btcssdd.jpg" alt="Crypto Fear and Greed Index Taps Low at 'Extreme Fear,' BTC Technicals Point to Uncertainty" width="1280" height="400" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-476273" class="wp-caption-text">Tradingview’s BTC/USD technicals, specifically oscillators and moving averages on July 21, 2021, at 12:00 p.m. (EDT).</figcaption></figure> 
  
  <p>
    All the moving average indicators suggest the “sell” range while the simple moving average (SMA 10) and the exponential moving average (EMA 10) are in the “buy” range. As far as BTC/USD oscillators, the only signal for “buy” is the momentum indicator but the moving average convergence divergence (MACD), a trend that follows momentum, is recorded as a “sell” on Wednesday.
  </p>
  
  <h2>
    Delta Exchange CEO Says ‘$30K Has Proven to Be Reliable Support Since May’
  </h2>
  
  <p>
    Meanwhile, despite the plunge on Tuesday morning, bitcoin (BTC) continues to hold a support zone. In a note sent to Bitcoin.com News, Delta Exchange CEO Pankaj Balani explains the current support, at least so far, has been reliable.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    “Bitcoin has been grinding lower since the start of this month,” Balani said. “Volatility has compressed significantly with a lower range. Bitcoin is trading in a significant support zone of $29 – $31K USDT. $30K has proven to be very reliable support since May. A breakdown of this level is likely to result in a significant increase in volatility and a final capitulation of crypto assets. That said, BTC is still in the $30K – $40K rectangle until a conclusive breakdown takes place,” the Delta Exchange executive added.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <em><strong>What do you think about bitcoin’s CFGI metric tapping “extreme fear” and the technicals from today’s Tradingview stats? Do you agree with Pankaj Balani’s reliable support comment? Let us know what you think about this subject in the comments section below.</strong></em>
  </p>
